ngles were a group of Anglian peoples in the east Midlands of England, around the Fens and the Nene and Welland valleys.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/middle-assyrian-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/middle-assyrian-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Middle Assyrian Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Middle Assyrian Empire was the phase of Assyrian history that began when Ashur-uballit I asserted independence from Mitanni in the fourteenth century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/middle-atlas"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/middle-atlas.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Middle Atlas</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Middle Atlas is a mountain range in central Morocco, part of the Atlas system, running north-east from the High Atlas towards the Taza gap.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/middle-bronze-age"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/middle-bronze-age.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Middle Bronze Age</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Middle Bronze Age is the archaeological period of roughly 2000 to 1550 BCE in the Levant.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/middle-east"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/middle-east.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Middle East</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Middle East is the region of western Asia and north-eastern Africa including the Levant, Mesopotamia, Arabia, Iran, Anatolia and Egypt.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/middle-egypt"><img clas